<title>USA: Pharmacopeia gets $5 mln payment from Akzo.</title>
<headline>Pharmacopeia gets $5 mln payment from Akzo.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmacopeia Inc said Friday that it has received a $5 million payment from Akzo Nobel NV's pharmaceutical business unit, NV Organon.</p>
<p>The payment, which consisted of a technology access fee and the second and final equity purchase, was in accordance with a collaborative drug discovery agreement.</p>
<p>The program focuses on undisclosed molecular targets in therapy for depression, anxiety, psychosis, and human reproduction.</p>
</text>
